{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>In all the way, etc., that you may live, and that it may be good for you, and that you may prolong, etc.</b> The meaning of ״תִּחְיוּן״ — length of days in this world; and His saying <b>and that it may be good for you</b> — the goodness of the World to Come; and His saying <b>and that you may prolong, etc.</b> — that Israel will never be exiled from the land." "And according to the reasoning of Rabbi Jacob (Kiddushin 39b), who said that there is no reward for a mitzvah in this world, it appears that Rabbi Jacob would concede regarding one who is a perfect righteous person and has kept the entire Torah, that he merits reward even in this world. For Rabbi Jacob spoke only of a person whose merits are a majority. And so you will find that they said there in Kiddushin, when they raised a difficulty from that baraita which stated: whoever's merits are a majority — they proclaim for him, etc., and the Gemara established it according to Rabbi Jacob." "<b>And from it</b> we may infer from what he said, 'whoever's merits are a majority' — you have learned that this speaks specifically of one who has transgressions in his hand, only that his merits are a majority; it is about him that it says, 'they proclaim for him,' etc. But one who is entirely merits, one must concede that HaShem will do good to him even in this world. And this is what it says: <b>in all the way that He commanded, etc.</b> — it was precise to say <b>בְּכָל</b> ('in all') to signal that it speaks of one who keeps everything; and for such a person there is reward in the World to Come, as His saying ״לְמַעַן תִּחְיוּן וְטוֹב״ etc., and there is also reward in this world, which is His saying <b>and that you may prolong days in the land which you shall possess</b> — and it did not say <b>and that you may prolong days</b> without specification, by which we would have explained that the intention is the World that is entirely long."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:35.580876674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}